    "result_text": "All tests pass with `BUILD SUCCESS`. Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## Changes\n\n**Identity key redesign** \u2014 now `SHA-256 hex over (normalizedTelephone + '|' + lowerEmail + '|' + soundex(lastName))`, returned as a full 64-char lowercase hex digest:\n\n- **`model/Soundex.java`** (new) \u2014 single definition of the American Soundex code (letter + 3 digits), with the standard h/w-transparent, vowel-resetting rules. Reused by both duplicate detection and the identity key.\n- **`model/Sha256.java`** \u2014 added `lowerHex(value)` (full 64-char lowercase digest) alongside the existing truncated `upperHex`, sharing one private `hex` helper.\n- **`model/OwnerIdentity.java`** \u2014 `key(telephone, email, lastName)` / `of(owner)` now hash `telephone | lowerEmail | soundex(lastName)` via `Sha256.lowerHex`. The response `identityKey` (via `OwnerMapper`) automatically picks this up.\n\n**Duplicate detection (409) on the single identity key:**\n- **`RejectDuplicateOwnerIdentity.java`** (new function) \u2014 throws `DuplicateOwnerException` when the candidate's identity key matches any **active** (non-deleted) owner's.\n- **`DuplicateOwnerException` / `DuplicateOwnerExceptionHandler`** + escalation YAML \u2014 checked exception \u2192 409 Conflict (mirroring `CityAtCapacityException`).\n- **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted `rejectDuplicateIdentity` right after `rejectDisposableEmail`, so the email-domain blocklist still runs first; and corrected the stale top comment.\n\n**Soft-match behaviour change** \u2014 **`AssignOwnerPossibleDuplicate.java`** now flags a soft match when the identity key *differs* but `soundex(lastName)` and postcode match (previously: same last name + postcode + different telephone). So two owners with the same surname/postcode but different telephones are now created as a soft match rather than rejected \u2014 the identity key is the single hard-duplicate gate.\n\n**Cleanup** \u2014 fixed a stale `{@link RejectDuplicateOwnerTelephone}` javadoc reference in `NormalizeOwnerTelephone`.\n\nThe behavioural note in the spec about a \"separate household-duplicate 409 block from the computed householdId\" \u2014 that block did not exist in this codebase (only the stale comment referenced it); `householdId` remains for household size/membership-cap logic, just no longer part of identity.\n\nTests: `AcceptanceTest` (`coreIdentityKeyIsSha256Hex`, `coreRejectsDuplicateIdentity`) and the full suite are green.",
